This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user asked me to build the cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, implementing it as the Angular application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`). The stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. The work is split into tickets in `spec/tickets/` (01 through 07) which must be implemented **in order**. `spec/README.md` is stated to be the complete specification: I was told not to ask any questions, and where the spec is silent I should choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task is finished only when every ticket is done AND `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. A hard USD budget cap applies to the session (started at $5; by the last check-in, ~$1.53 remained), so I have been deliberately economical — doing the implementation work myself directly rather than delegating heavily to subagents, and using lightweight external tooling (not modifying the project's dependencies) for browser verification.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo; Angular 22 standalone, zoneless app (`provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners`, no NgModules), SCSS, Vitest (unit tests), ESLint.
   - Angular Material 22 + CDK installed; Material theme via `@use '@angular/material' as mat;` in `styles.scss` (azure palette); native date adapter provided for `MatDatepicker`.
   - **Critical constraint discovered**: `@angular/animations` package is NOT installed in node_modules at all. Neither `provideAnimationsAsync()` (lazy `import('@angular/animations/browser')`) nor `provideNoopAnimations()`/`BrowserAnimationsModule` (static `import ... from '@angular/animations/browser'`) can be used — both fail to resolve at build time. Per spec ("Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed."), the fix was to provide **no animations provider at all**; Material components function without animations (just no transition effects).
   - Backend: `json-server` 0.17.4 serving `db.json` from workspace root at `http://localhost:3000` (hardcoded base URL per spec, must not change). `pnpm api` starts it. CORS enabled.
   - Data model: `Movie {id, title, genre, runtimeMinutes, format: 'PL dubbing'|'PL subtitles'}`; `Screening {id, movieId, date: 'YYYY-MM-DD', time: 'HH:mm', occupiedSeats: string[]}`; `Reservation {id, screeningId, seats: string[], customer: {firstName,lastName,email,phone}, totalPrice}`. Seat identifier format `R<row>C<column>`; a couch occupies two identifiers (e.g. row 15 columns 5-6 → `R15C5`+`R15C6`).
   - Routes (Angular Router, lazy-loaded standalone components via `loadComponent`): `/` (movie list), `/screenings/:id/seats`, `/screenings/:id/summary` (guarded), `/screenings/:id/checkout` (guarded), `/confirmation` (guarded), `**` → redirect to `/`.
   - Booking state persisted in `sessionStorage` (key `cinescope-booking`) as a single JSON blob: `{screeningId, seats: string[], form: {firstName,lastName,email,confirmEmail,phone,terms}, paid: boolean, customerEmail: string|null}`. Managed via Angular **signals** (not RxJS state) in `BookingService`, since the app is zoneless and signal mutations drive change detection directly.
   - Functional route guards (`CanActivateFn`) for booking-state gating (`activeBookingGuard`, `paidBookingGuard`).
   - CSS Grid-based auditorium layout: 28 grid-column tracks per row (label-left, 4 seat tracks, 1 aisle track, 16 seat tracks, 1 aisle track, 4 seat tracks, label-right), computed via a `trackForColumn(column)` helper, to render the 15-row/24-column auditorium with two 2-seat-wide aisles (between columns 4/5 and 20/21), an "entrance" empty gap (rows 1-10, columns 1-4, rendered as nothing — explicitly NOT an aisle element), accessible seats (row 1, columns 10-15), and 12 couches in row 15 (column pairs 1-2, 3-4, …, 23-24).
   - Pricing: rows 1-5 → 25.00 PLN, rows 6-10 → 32.00 PLN, rows 11-14 → 39.00 PLN, couches (row 15) → 89.00 PLN flat (not per seat).
   - Toast via `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent()` with a custom `Toast` component whose template root has `data-testid="toast"` (to satisfy the UI-library requirement for toasts while controlling the exact DOM contract); 4000ms duration, one-at-a-time (MatSnackBar's default behavior already replaces any open snack bar).
   - `data-testid` / `data-*` attribute contract (section 9 of spec) must be followed exactly — verified several of these already via Playwright locators.
   - Angular `toSignal()` (rxjs-interop) used to bridge `ActivatedRoute.queryParamMap` into a signal; `effect()` used in `MovieList` constructor to refetch movies/screenings whenever the computed `effectiveDate` signal changes.
   - Browser-automation verification tooling: `playwright-core` (installed standalone in a scratch dir `/tmp/pw-test`, NOT added to the project's package.json) driving a **pre-cached** Chromium binary at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome` (launched with `args: ['--no-sandbox']`), since no `chromium-cli` tool was available and installing the full `playwright` package with browser download was avoided (binaries already cached).
   - Environment quirk: in my sandboxed Bash tool, backend/dev servers are reachable via `http://[::1]:PORT` but NOT via `http://localhost:PORT` from Node's `fetch` — likely a Bash-tool-specific loopback restriction, not necessarily reflective of the actual browser runtime environment (the real system/browser DID resolve `localhost` fine when Playwright's Chromium hit `http://localhost:4200` and `http://localhost:3000` directly).
   - Faking the browser clock for tests: `page.addInitScript()` overriding the global `Date` constructor (subclassing it so parameterized `new Date(y,m,d)` calls still work normally, but zero-arg `new Date()`/`Date.now()` return a fixed timestamp) — used to test against db.json's Sept 15-21, 2026 screening data despite the sandbox's real "today" being 2026-10-20. This is a test-harness-only technique; it does not touch app code and does not violate the spec's "do not change the date logic" instruction.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   **Spec files read (not modified)**: `spec/README.md` (full spec, read in full — contains sections 1-11: project setup, backend/data model/endpoints, screens & navigation & booking lifecycle & toasts & date formats, movie list spec, seat selection spec (auditorium geometry, selecting seats, colours/legend, prices, selected-seats panel, actions), summary spec, checkout spec, confirmation spec, element identifiers/data-testid contract (9.1-9.7), acceptance criteria AC-01 through AC-69, out-of-scope list), `spec/stack.md`, `spec/tickets/README.md`, and all of `spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md` through `07-final-pass.md` (ticket breakdowns with their own checkbox ACs, read in full via a single `cat` of all ticket files).

   **Existing scaffold files read**: `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`, `app.routes.ts`, `app.ts`, `app.html`, `app.spec.ts`, `src/styles.scss`, `src/main.ts`, `apps/cinescope/project.json`, root `package.json` (deps list — confirms `@angular/cdk`, `@angular/common`, `@angular/compiler`, `@angular/core`, `@angular/forms`, `@angular/material`, `@angular/platform-browser`, `@angular/router`, `rxjs` as deps; `@angular/build`, `@angular/cli`, `@angular/compiler-cli`, `vitest`, `json-server`, `sass`, `typescript`, `eslint` etc. as devDeps — notably **no** `@angular/animations`), and `db.json` (5 movies, screenings only for dates 2026-09-15 through 2026-09-21).

   **New directories created**: `apps/cinescope/src/app/{models,services,guards,utils,pages/movie-list,pages/seat-selection,pages/summary,pages/checkout,pages/confirmation,shared/toast}`.

   **Models**:
   - `models/movie.model.ts` — `Movie` interface matching spec exactly.
   - `models/screening.model.ts` — `Screening` interface.
   - `models/reservation.model.ts` — `Customer`, `Reservation`, `ReservationRequest` interfaces.
   - `models/booking.model.ts` — `CheckoutFormValues` interface (`firstName,lastName,email,confirmEmail,phone,terms`), `BookingState` interface (`screeningId,seats,form,paid,customerEmail`), plus `emptyCheckoutForm()` and `emptyBooking(screeningId)` factory functions.

   **Utils**:
   - `utils/seat.util.ts` — `seatId(row,col)`, `parseSeatId(id)`, `isAccessibleSeat(row,col)` (row===1 && col 10-15), `isCouchRow(row)` (row===15), `priceForRow(row)` (25/32/39/89 tiers), `formatPrice(price)` (`"25.00 PLN"`), `couchColumns(seatA,seatB)` (sorted tuple).
   - `utils/date.util.ts` — `toIsoDate`, `startOfDay`, `isValidIsoDate` (strict `YYYY-MM-DD` regex + round-trip check), `parseIsoDate`, `addDays`, `weekdayName`, `formatShowDate(isoDate,time)` → `"<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>"` e.g. `"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00"`.
   - `utils/selection.util.ts` — shared grouping logic used by both seat-selection and summary pages:
     ```ts
     export interface SelectionUnit {
       ids: string[];
       row: number;
       columns: number[];
       isCouch: boolean;
       price: number;
     }
     export function groupIntoUnits(seatIds: string[]): SelectionUnit[] { ... }
     export function unitSeatLabel(unit: SelectionUnit): string {
       return unit.isCouch ? `Couch ${unit.columns[0]}-${unit.columns[1]}` : `${unit.columns[0]}`;
     }
     ```
     `groupIntoUnits` deduplicates couch id-pairs (row 15, pairing column with its partner via odd/even check), sorts ids within a couch unit ascending by column, and sorts the overall array by row then first column.

   **Services**:
   - `services/api.service.ts` — `ApiService` wrapping `HttpClient` against `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`: `getMovies()`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreenings({date?, movieId?})` (via `HttpParams`), `getScreening(id)`, `createReservation(request)`.
   - `services/booking.service.ts` — `BookingService`, fully signal-based with manual `sessionStorage` persistence (key `cinescope-booking`):
     ```ts
     @Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
     export class BookingService {
       private readonly state = signal<BookingState | null>(this.load());
       readonly booking = this.state.asReadonly();
       private load(): BookingState | null { ... }
       private persist(value: BookingState | null): void { this.state.set(value); sessionStorage.setItem/.removeItem(...); }
       ensureBookingForScreening(screeningId: number): void { /* keep if unpaid & same screeningId, else emptyBooking */ }
       hasActiveBookingFor(screeningId: number): boolean { /* !paid && same id && seats.length>0 */ }
       hasPaidBooking(): boolean { return !!this.state()?.paid; }
       isSeatSelected(id: string): boolean { ... }
       seatCount(): number { ... }
       toggleUnit(ids: string[]): boolean { /* true=ok, false=would exceed 10-seat cap; returns true also on successful deselect */ }
       removeUnit(ids: string[]): void { ... }
       updateForm(partial: Partial<CheckoutFormValues>): void { ... }
       markPaid(email: string): void { ... }
       clear(): void { this.persist(null); }
     }
     ```
     Verified via unit tests (see below) including the cap-of-10 logic and couch-counts-as-2 logic, plus cross-instance sessionStorage persistence.
   - `services/toast.service.ts` — `ToastService.show(message)` calling `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent(Toast, {data:{message}, duration:4000, horizontalPosition:'center', verticalPosition:'bottom'})`.

   **Shared**:
   - `shared/toast/toast.ts` — `Toast` component: `template: '<span data-testid="toast">{{ message }}</span>'`, reads `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA` via `inject()`.

   **Guards**:
   - `guards/booking.guard.ts`:
     ```ts
     export const activeBookingGuard: CanActivateFn = (route) => {
       const bookingService = inject(BookingService);
       const router = inject(Router);
       const screeningId = Number(route.paramMap.get('id'));
       return bookingService.hasActiveBookingFor(screeningId) ? true : router.parseUrl('/');
     };
     export const paidBookingGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
       const bookingService = inject(BookingService);
       const router = inject(Router);
       return bookingService.hasPaidBooking() ? true : router.parseUrl('/');
     };
     ```

   **App shell/config**:
   - `app.routes.ts` — rewritten with 6 routes: `''` (MovieList, lazy), `'screenings/:id/seats'` (SeatSelection, lazy, no guard — component itself redirects on load failure), `'screenings/:id/summary'` (Summary, lazy, `canActivate: [activeBookingGuard]`), `'screenings/:id/checkout'` (Checkout, lazy, same guard), `'confirmation'` (Confirmation, lazy, `canActivate: [paidBookingGuard]`), `'**'` → `redirectTo: ''`.
   - `app.config.ts` — final version (after removing animations provider due to the build error):
     ```ts
     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';
     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';
     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';
     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';

     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
       providers: [provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(), provideRouter(appRoutes), provideNativeDateAdapter(), provideHttpClient()],
     };
     ```

   **Pages — Movie List** (`pages/movie-list/`):
   - `movie-list.ts` — `MovieList` component. Computes `today`/`todayIso` once; `rawDateParam = toSignal(route.queryParamMap, {initialValue: route.snapshot.queryParamMap})`; `effectiveDate = computed(...)` (valid ISO && `>= todayIso` else today); `fiveDayIsoDates` (today+0..4); `dayButtons` computed (labels `'Today'` then full weekday names); `datepickerValue` computed (null when effectiveDate is one of the five, else parsed Date); `loading`/`error` signals; `movies`/`screenings` signals; `cards` computed (filter movies with ≥1 screening that day, screenings sorted by time string). Constructor uses `effect(() => this.loadFor(this.effectiveDate()))` to fetch on init and whenever the date changes (refetches both `/movies` and `/screenings?date=`). `selectDate(date)` navigates with `queryParams: {date}`; `openSeats(screeningId)` navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats`.
   - `movie-list.html` — day-picker (`data-testid="day-picker"` container, `day-button` ×5 with `data-date`/`data-selected`, `mat-stroked-button`), `mat-form-field` + `input[matInput][matDatepicker]` with `data-testid="date-picker"`, `readonly` attribute on the date input; loading/error/empty/loaded `@if/@else if` chain with exact testids (`movies-loading`, `movies-error`+`movies-retry-button`, `movies-empty`, `movie-list`/`movie-card`/`movie-title`/`movie-genre`/`movie-runtime`/`movie-format`/`screening-button`).
   - `movie-list.scss` — basic layout styling (max-width 960px, flex day-picker, card list).

   **Pages — Seat Selection** (`pages/seat-selection/`):
   - `seat-layout.ts` — pure layout generator:
     ```ts
     export type SeatCell =
       | { kind: 'aisle'; track: number }
       | { kind: 'seat'; column: number; track: number; accessible: boolean }
       | { kind: 'couch'; start: number; end: number; track: number };
     export interface SeatRow { row: number; cells: SeatCell[]; }
     const AISLE_1_TRACK = 6; const AISLE_2_TRACK = 23;
     export function trackForColumn(column: number): number {
       if (column <= 4) return column + 1;
       if (column <= 20) return column + 2;
       return column + 3;
     }
     export function buildAuditoriumRows(): SeatRow[] { /* rows 1-15; row 15 = 12 couches; rows 1-10 start at column 5, rows 11-14 start at column 1; cells sorted by track */ }
     ```
   - `seat-selection.ts` — `SeatSelection` component. Reads `screeningId` from route snapshot; `rows = buildAuditoriumRows()` (static); `screening` signal; `occupied`/`selected` computed `Set<string>`; `subtitle` computed (`"Show Date: ..."` via `formatShowDate`); `legendItems` (available/selected/unavailable/accessible with labels); `selectedCount`/`selectedRowLines` computed (uses shared `groupIntoUnits`, builds `Row <r>: <labels>` lines grouped+sorted); `canContinue` computed (`selectedCount()>0`). Constructor subscribes to `api.getScreening(screeningId)`; on success sets `screening` signal and calls `bookingService.ensureBookingForScreening(screeningId)`; on error `router.navigateByUrl('/')`. Methods: `seatState(row,cell)`/`couchState(row,cell)` (unavailable/selected/accessible/available precedence), `stateColor(state)` (maps to the 4 hex colors), `onSeatClick`/`onCouchClick` (ignore if unavailable, else `toggle(ids)` → `bookingService.toggleUnit(ids)`, shows toast `'Maximum 10 seats per booking'` if it returns false), `cancel()` (clear booking + navigate `/`), `continue()` (guarded by `canContinue()`, navigates to summary). Note: deliberately does NOT fetch the movie (only the screening) since nothing on this screen displays movie info — a conscious simplification given the spec's ACs for this screen don't require it.
   - `seat-selection.html` — title/subtitle/seat-limit-info, `screen-indicator`, `seat-map` with `@for` over rows/cells rendering `row-label-left`/`aisle`/`seat`/`couch`/`row-label-right` via `@switch`, inline `[style.grid-column]` and `[style.background-color]` bindings, `legend`/`legend-item` loop, `selected-seats` panel, `cancel-button`/`continue-button`.
   - `seat-selection.scss` — 28-track CSS grid (`$label:24px; $seat:30px; $aisle:64px;` → `grid-template-columns: $label repeat(4,$seat) $aisle repeat(16,$seat) $aisle repeat(4,$seat) $label`), legend/swatch styling, centered layout.
   - `seat-layout.spec.ts` — vitest tests (initially had `any` lint warnings, fixed by adding an `isSeat` type guard): verifies 15 rows, 308 total selectable elements, rows 1-10 have 20 seats (columns 5-24), rows 11-14 have 24 seats, row 15 has 12 couches and 0 seats, row 1 accessible columns are exactly [10,11,12,13,14,15], every row has exactly 2 aisles.

   **Pages — Summary** (`pages/summary/`):
   - `summary.ts` — `Summary` component. `screeningId` from route; `screening`/`movie` signals; `dateTime`/`movieTitle` computed; `items` computed (via `groupIntoUnits` + `unitSeatLabel` + `formatPrice`); `total`/`totalLabel` computed (`"Total: <sum.toFixed(2)> PLN"`). Constructor: nested subscribe — `api.getScreening(id)` then `api.getMovie(screening.movieId)`; redirects to `/` on either failure. `remove(item)` calls `bookingService.removeUnit(item.ids)`, navigates to seat map if booking becomes empty. `back()`/`confirm()` navigate accordingly.
   - `summary.html` — `summary-title`, `summary-list`/`summary-item` (`summary-item-title`/`-datetime`/`-row`/`-seat`/`-price`/`-remove-button`), `summary-total`, `back-button`/`confirm-button`.
   - `summary.scss` — basic card-list styling.

   **Pages — Checkout** (`pages/checkout/`) — **currently the focus of an active bug investigation**:
   - `checkout.ts` — `Checkout` component (current state after my non-null-assertion lint fix):
     ```ts
     type FieldName = 'firstName' | 'lastName' | 'email' | 'confirmEmail' | 'phone' | 'terms';
     const EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
     const PHONE_PATTERN = /^\d{9}$/;

     @Component({ selector: 'app-checkout', imports: [MatButtonModule, MatCheckboxModule, MatFormFieldModule, MatInputModule], templateUrl: './checkout.html', styleUrl: './checkout.scss' })
     export class Checkout {
       private readonly api = inject(ApiService);
       private readonly route = inject(ActivatedRoute);
       private readonly router = inject(Router);
       private readonly bookingService = inject(BookingService);
       private readonly toast = inject(ToastService);
       private readonly screeningId = Number(this.route.snapshot.paramMap.get('id'));

       readonly submitting = signal(false);
       private readonly touched = signal<Record<FieldName, boolean>>({ firstName:false,lastName:false,email:false,confirmEmail:false,phone:false,terms:false });

       readonly values = computed<CheckoutFormValues>(() => this.bookingService.booking()?.form ?? emptyCheckoutForm());

       readonly total = computed(() => groupIntoUnits(this.bookingService.booking()?.seats ?? []).reduce((sum, unit) => sum + unit.price, 0));
       readonly payLabel = computed(() => `Pay ${formatPrice(this.total())}`);

       private readonly allErrors = computed(() => this.computeErrors(this.values()));

       readonly errors = computed(() => {
         const touched = this.touched();
         const all = this.allErrors();
         return { firstName: touched.firstName?all.firstName:null, lastName: touched.lastName?all.lastName:null, email: touched.email?all.email:null, confirmEmail: touched.confirmEmail?all.confirmEmail:null, phone: touched.phone?all.phone:null, terms: touched.terms?all.terms:null };
       });

       private computeErrors(values: CheckoutFormValues): Record<FieldName, string | null> {
         return {
           firstName: values.firstName===''?'First name is required':values.firstName.length<2?'First name must be at least 2 characters':null,
           lastName: values.lastName===''?'Last name is required':values.lastName.length<2?'Last name must be at least 2 characters':null,
           email: values.email===''?'Email is required':!EMAIL_PATTERN.test(values.email)?'Enter a valid email address':null,
           confirmEmail: values.confirmEmail===''?'Confirm email is required':values.confirmEmail!==values.email?'Email addresses do not match':null,
           phone: values.phone===''?null:!PHONE_PATTERN.test(values.phone)?'Phone number must be exactly 9 digits':null,
           terms: values.terms?null:'You must accept the terms and conditions',
         };
       }

       update(field: FieldName, value: string): void { this.bookingService.updateForm({ [field]: value } as Partial<CheckoutFormValues>); }
       markTouched(field: FieldName): void { this.touched.update((t) => ({ ...t, [field]: true })); }
       toggleTerms(checked: boolean): void { this.bookingService.updateForm({ terms: checked }); this.markTouched('terms'); }
       back(): void { this.router.navigate(['/screenings', this.screeningId, 'summary']); }

       pay(): void {
         if (this.submitting()) return;
         const values = this.values();
         const errors = this.computeErrors(values);
         const valid = Object.values(errors).every((e) => e === null);
         if (!valid) {
           this.touched.set({ firstName:true,lastName:true,email:true,confirmEmail:true,phone:true,terms:true });
           this.toast.show('The form contains errors');
           return;
         }
         const seats = groupIntoUnits(this.bookingService.booking()?.seats ?? []).flatMap((unit) => unit.ids);
         this.submitting.set(true);
         this.api.createReservation({ screeningId: this.screeningId, seats, customer: {firstName:values.firstName,lastName:values.lastName,email:values.email,phone:values.phone}, totalPrice: this.total() }).subscribe({
           next: () => { this.bookingService.markPaid(values.email); this.router.navigateByUrl('/confirmation'); },
           error: () => { this.submitting.set(false); this.toast.show('Payment failed. Please try again.'); },
         });
       }
     }
     ```
